      <p class="text-blue-50 text-lg mb-8 leading-relaxed">
        Converting <strong>calories to kilojoules</strong> (and vice versa) is a simple mathematical process once you know the exact conversion factor. Understanding this formula is incredibly helpful when comparing products from different countries or using international fitness applications. The internationally recognized scientific conversion rate is straightforward:
      </p>
      
      <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-6 justify-center items-center mb-10">
        <div class="bg-surface/10 backdrop-blur-md rounded-2xl p-8 w-full text-center border border-white/20 transform transition duration-300 hover:scale-105">
          <span class="block text-blue-100 text-sm uppercase tracking-wider mb-3 font-semibold">Calories to kJ</span>
          <span class="text-4xl font-bold font-mono tracking-tight">1 kcal = 4.184 kJ</span>
          <p class="text-sm text-blue-200 mt-3">Multiply your calories by 4.184</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-surface/10 backdrop-blur-md rounded-2xl p-8 w-full text-center border border-white/20 transform transition duration-300 hover:scale-105">
          <span class="block text-blue-100 text-sm uppercase tracking-wider mb-3 font-semibold">kJ to Calories</span>
          <span class="text-4xl font-bold font-mono tracking-tight">1 kJ = 0.239 kcal</span>
          <p class="text-sm text-blue-200 mt-3">Multiply your kilojoules by 0.239 (or divide by 4.184)</p>
        </div>
      </div>

